    <string name="help_start_end_q">What happens at the start and end?</string>
    <string name="help_start_end_a">Airplane mode turns on at the start and off at the end. The app only undoes what it changed, so if airplane mode was already on, it stays on, and if you turned it off midway, it stays off.</string>
    <string name="help_wifi_q">What do the Wi-Fi options do?</string>
    <string name="help_wifi_a">“Turn off Wi-Fi at start” turns Wi-Fi off before airplane mode. “Turn on Wi-Fi at end” turns it back on, but only if the app turned it off.</string>
    <string name="help_overnight_q">Which day is an overnight schedule on?</string>
    <!-- %1$s is 11 PM and %2$s is 7 AM. -->
    <string name="help_overnight_a">The day it starts. A Friday schedule from %1$s to %2$s ends on Saturday morning.</string>
    <string name="help_once_q">What if I pick no days?</string>
    <string name="help_once_a">The schedule runs once at its next start time, then switches itself off. If you switch it on between its start and end, it starts right away.</string>
    <string name="help_skip_q">Can I skip or delay a schedule?</string>
    <string name="help_skip_a">In the hour before a schedule starts, you can skip it, or postpone it to start later and still end on time.</string>
    <string name="help_pause_q">Can I take a break during a schedule?</string>
    <string name="help_pause_a">Yes. Pause it to turn airplane mode off for a while, or end it early. Postpone and pause share one length, which you can change or turn off in Settings.</string>
    <string name="help_change_active_q">Do changes apply right away?</string>
    <string name="help_change_active_a">Yes. Switching off or deleting a running schedule ends it, like a normal end. Switching on or adding one that covers the current time starts it. Editing the times starts or ends it to match.</string>
    <string name="help_overlap_q">Why can\'t schedules overlap?</string>
    <string name="help_overlap_a">Only one schedule can be in charge at a time. Back-to-back schedules act as one, so airplane mode stays on in between. Wi-Fi follows the first one\'s start option and the last one\'s end option.</string>
    <string name="help_missed_q">Why didn\'t airplane mode switch?</string>
    <string name="help_missed_a">Shizuku wasn\'t running or allowed, or the phone was off. By design, the app doesn\'t catch up on its own, but if notifications are allowed, you\'ll get an alert.</string>
    <string name="help_missed_a_sui">Sui wasn\'t allowed, or the phone was off. By design, the app doesn\'t catch up on its own, but if notifications are allowed, you\'ll get an alert.</string>
    <string name="help_missed_a_root">Root access wasn\'t allowed, or the phone was off. By design, the app doesn\'t catch up on its own, but if notifications are allowed, you\'ll get an alert.</string>
    <!-- Shown below Android 12 only. -->
    <string name="help_late_q">Why did a schedule run late?</string>
    <string name="help_late_a">Battery optimization can delay it by up to 2 hours if you rarely open the app. Tap the battery warning on the Schedules screen to turn it off for Airplane Scheduler.</string>
    <string name="help_shizuku_stopped_q">Why does Shizuku keep stopping?</string>
    <string name="help_shizuku_stopped_a">Shizuku stops whenever the phone restarts. If notifications are allowed, you\'ll get a warning an hour before a schedule.</string>
    <!-- Added to the answer above below Android 11, which lacks wireless debugging. -->
    <string name="help_shizuku_stopped_legacy">On this Android version, starting Shizuku needs a computer or root.</string>
    <string name="help_root_q">Can I use root?</string>
    <string name="help_root_a">Yes. In Settings, set Permission mode to Root, and the app won\'t need Shizuku.</string>

